## Decision

This folder should remain the program’s evidence and decision register. It contains shared reviews, historical packages and ownership maps, not a seventeenth research contribution. The current assessment finds four projects worth focused proof/priority work, three conditional research projects, one deferred empirical direction, and seven exposition/companion/correction projects. Those categories concern the next useful form of work, not guaranteed publication or rejection.

The old “high uniqueness” classifications chiefly answered whether local folders had been separated into distinct ownership units. They did not establish novelty against published literature. The new decisions intentionally narrow several of them. A coherent technical article can remain useful after a broad research-paper claim is removed.

## Portfolio reasoning

BT has a specific incidence/collapse characterization with sharp boundary examples. P01 has a coherent chain-ring classification tying support, coding and raw teleportation to different Smith invariants. FJ has a compact finite-jet/regularity synthesis whose novelty may be modest but worth checking. P02 has fully quantified exact-query limitations under a carefully stated access model. These are the strongest candidates because their central statements can be compared directly with prior theorems and potentially survive without the surrounding CM/ProLT branding.

GU needs a meaningful guard library and application beyond the four-region worked example. GR has a corrected observation-cover formulation and a real safety-composition issue, but needs a constrained problem with a new result. CO needs alignment between the paper and actual implementation plus a matched cost model. SC should wait for a specific endpoint and evidence of recoverable headroom before another selection/decomposition campaign.

FO and PL are best treated as exposition/specification unless a new use establishes more. IP, SP, PC and BR provide algebraic and operational companions whose value lies partly in keeping models distinct. AU is a correctness and regression resource. Their usefulness does not require inventing a separate novelty claim for every shared lemma.

## Evidence and confidence

The review used current manuscript sources, selected historical variants, existing referee/agent findings, local ownership evidence and targeted primary-source literature searches. This is one assistant’s analytical review, not a panel of independent human experts. Selected proofs were examined in detail; no blanket claim of full formal verification is made. Abstract-only comparisons are labelled as such in the literature ledger. Search non-detection never establishes firstness.

The fresh bounded checker independently enumerates five Z/4 support models, tests the corrected observation-cover formulation on 382 order pairs through four vertices, reproduces two refinement homology examples, verifies 35 small Boolean evaluation-rank cases, and checks selected ring/guard facts. Its script, results and scope are preserved here. It is not a performance benchmark, a replay of every archive, or a proof of the general manuscript theorems.

The new reviews preserve all existing manuscripts, reports and archives. Historical source manifests and the earlier partition receipt remain dated snapshots; they are not rewritten to suggest that the new research reviews existed at the old commit. Each new review directory has its own manifest, and a new publication-workspace verification receipt records the additive change.

## How to use the decisions

Use PORTFOLIO_DECISIONS.md for the ordered reading list. Each project has one RESEARCH_ASSESSMENT.md and DECISION.json with its central claim, overlap boundary, prior-art comparison, proposed extensions, success conditions and stopping rule. INPUT_EVIDENCE.json records paths and hashes for provenance. LITERATURE_LEDGER.json records access depth and URLs. SEARCH_LOG.md explains search coverage and unresolved areas. The portable check script documents exactly what the fresh numerical evidence means.

Do not start sixteen publication campaigns. First review BT and P01 individually and decide whether to commission independent specialist proof/priority review. Then examine FJ and P02. Conditional projects should pass their small gates before large implementation or empirical work. Companion material can be edited when its main owner paper actually needs it.

This assessment does not authorize manuscript rewrites, commits, pushes, external submissions or new experimental spending. It completes the requested decision preparation and leaves the research choices for the planned project-by-project discussion.

## Evidence and review limits

Project register; partition/claim-ownership and pairwise evidence; attached preservation/consolidation audits; shared archives and new bounded verification.

This is a research triage and selected proof review by one assistant, not an independent expert panel, exhaustive prior-art clearance, acceptance prediction or formal proof certification. Existing agent findings were treated as evidence to check. Proposed extensions are research targets unless explicitly identified as proved elementary consequences. No manuscript is modified by this assessment.

